--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Wake Vision (training, validation and test images, person labels, and the
lighting flags used in the accuracy breakdown)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Harvard Edge Computing Lab, "Wake Vision"
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/Harvard-Edge/Wake-Vision
  Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

  Banbury, C., Njor, E., Garavagno, A. M., Stewart, M., Warden, P.,
  Kudlur, M., Jeffries, N., Fafoutis, X., Reddi, V. J.
  "Wake Vision: A Tailored Dataset and Benchmark Suite for TinyML
  Computer Vision Applications", 2024. arXiv:2405.00892.

  The dataset was used as published; the only change made here is
  the preprocessing described in dataset/README.md (every image centre-
  cropped to a square and resized). No modification of the dataset itself
  is redistributed here.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Open Images (bounding-box annotations, from which the "near person" labels
are derived)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Google LLC, "Open Images Dataset" (V4 to V7 annotation files)
  https://storage.googleapis.com/openimages/web/index.html
  Licence of the annotations: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
  (CC BY 4.0)

  Kuznetsova, A., Rom, H., Alldrin, N., Uijlings, J., Krasin, I.,
  Pont-Tuset, J., Kamali, S., Popov, S., Malloci, M., Kolesnikov, A.,
  Duerig, T., Ferrari, V. "The Open Images Dataset V4: Unified image
  classification, object detection, and visual relationship detection at
  scale", International Journal of Computer Vision, 2020.

  Changes made: the person boxes were intersected with the same centre crop
  applied to the images and reduced to one of three distance classes
  (dataset/prepare_dataset.py). These derived labels are not redistributed;
  the scripts recreate them from the published annotation files.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
The images themselves
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Wake Vision's images come from Open Images, which collected them from
  Flickr. Each photograph carries its own Creative Commons licence, chosen by
  the photographer, and the Hugging Face release of Wake Vision does not
  carry per-image attribution. For that reason no image, image cache or
  sample derived from the dataset is included in this repository: the
  scripts in dataset/ download the data from its publishers at run time,
  and anything they write is git-ignored. Anyone who runs them is
  responsible for complying with the licences of the images they download.

